.TH tufile n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tufile
.PP
Magic\-signature file type detection in pure Tcl, like Unix \fBfile\fR, with a user\-extensible signature table and extension\-mismatch checking. Reads only the file header.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tufile 0.1
.CE
.SS API
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::detect path\fR        \-> dict of the most specific match, or empty dict
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::type path\fR          \-> short name (\fBpng\fR, \fBpdf\fR, \fBodt\fR, ...) or \fB""\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::mime path\fR          \-> MIME type or \fB""\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::describe path\fR      \-> human\-readable description or \fB"data"\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::checkExtension path\fR\-> dict \fB{path detected declared expected status}\fR with \fBstatus\fR in \fBok | mismatch | noext | unknown | unknownext\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::register name \-offset N (\-hex HEX | \-ascii STR) \-mime M \-ext {e ...} \-desc D\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::loadFile path\fR      \-> load signatures from a text file (returns count)
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::forget name\fR / \fBtufile::reset\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBtufile::signatures\fR         \-> list of signature names
.PP
Signature file format (one per line, \fB#\fR comments, \fB|\fR\-separated):
.CS
# name | offset | marker | mime | ext1,ext2 | description
foofmt | 0 | @FOO!   | application/x-foo | foo,fo | Foo format
barfmt | 4 | CAFE    | application/x-bar | bar    | Bar format
.CE
.PP
A leading \fB@\fR marks the marker as ASCII text; otherwise it is hex.
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tufile.tcl file                 # describe, like Unix file
tclsh bin/tufile.tcl check *.jpg          # extension vs content
tclsh bin/tufile.tcl -sigs my.txt type x.bin
.CE
.SS Scope
.PP
Offset + exact byte pattern match model (no masks, ranges, or nested rules like libmagic). ODT/ODS/ODP are recognized via the offset\-30 \fBmimetype\fR marker; DOCX/XLSX/PPTX share only the ZIP magic and are reported as \fBzip\fR.
